course: dictionary
lesson: 12885
title: The word entity
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An entity is a single thing that exists on its own, with its own identity. «A country is an entity with its own government and borders.» The clues are «its own government» and «its own borders», so an entity is a whole thing that is separate from others.
explain: You will meet entity in science, business, games and stories. It is a formal word, used when you want to talk about a thing without saying exactly what kind it is. «The club is a separate entity from the school.» The club is its own organisation, not part of the school.
explain: Entity can mean almost anything that exists. «In the game, every entity is a character or an object.» A player, a tree or a treasure chest can all be entities. In a spooky story, «the entity» is an unknown being that nobody can explain.
fact: An entity is a thing that exists as a separate, single whole.
fact: «Entity» is a noun, and its plural is «entities».
fact: In law and business, a «legal entity» is an organisation treated as one unit, such as a company.
fact: In computing and stories, an entity can be a character, an object or a mysterious creature.
fact: A good check is to swap in «thing» and see if the sentence still makes sense; «entity» is simply a more formal word.
exercise: «A country is an entity with its own government and borders.» What is an entity here? | A loud shout | A type of fruit | A sort of weather | *A single thing that exists on its own
exercise: «The company is a legal entity, so it can own land and sign contracts.» What does legal entity suggest? | A long, boring meeting | *An organisation treated as one unit | A person who is a lawyer
exercise: In a computer game, what can an entity be? | *A character or object | A recipe | A bus timetable | A cloud
test: «The ghost was a strange entity that nobody could explain.» What kind of thing is the ghost called here? | A bright star | A cooking pot | An old map | *An unknown being
test: Which is the plural of entity? | entityes | entitys | entity's | *entities
exam: Which best explains why a school can be called an entity? | *It is a single organisation with its own identity | It only exists at night | It is a kind of sweet | It is always painted blue
